v0.10.2 (2026-08-??)

Features and improvements
  - increased view distance
  - bundled DOOM1 shareware is now the v1.9 one
  - entering a level now shows "Entering <level name>" on screen.
    - the name is the WAD's own CWILV/WILV graphic where it has one for that
      level, as drawn on the original's intermission screen
    - otherwise it comes from the WAD's own MAPINFO if it has one,
      otherwise from the hard-coded level titles from vanilla
    - a PWAD map with neither is named after the file it came from
    - the menu's level list shows those names too
  - leaving a level now shows an intermission popup
    - it now also tracks your best time per level, and announces a new one
    - records are kept per WAD, level and difficulty, and survive a reload
    - the WAD is identified by a hash of its contents, so renaming a file
      keeps its records and two different WADs sharing a name don't collide
    - a run started with ?pos= can't set a record
  - a locked door or switch now says which key it wants

Fixed bugs
  - projectiles now collide the way vanilla's do
    - rockets, plasma and BFG balls hit whatever they actually fly into,
      re-checked every frame
    - every shot is now tested against each monster's real size instead of
      one shared 24-unit hitbox
    - monster fireballs no longer hit from a body-width away or from far
      over your head
    - a shot passing you at speed can no longer slip between two frames
  - fixed periods, commas, hyphens and underscores in on-screen WAD-font text
  - fixed stuck monsters
  - fixed the game freezing when a second WAD is started from the menu after
    already having played a level


===============================================================================

v0.10.1 (2026-08-09)

Features and improvements
  - camera and mouse controls
    - right-dragging no longer turns the camera
    - camera distance (+/-) and tilt ([/]) are no longer dev-mode only
    - the freed right mouse button is now bindable: switch to your previous
      weapon (the default), use, or nothing
  - the M mute key is gone - the volume slider at 0% is the same thing
  - menu cleanup
    - controls settings/overview built-in
    - Level and Difficulty share a row
    - dropped the subtitle under the title; the version number sits at the
      right end of the title row instead of the corner of the screen

Fixed bugs
  - stepping off a teleport destination pad no longer teleports you straight
    back: a teleport line crossed from its back side is ignored
  - fixed a sector that both changes light and moves, never showing its light
    on its own floor and wall
  - monster melee fixes (again...)
    - monsters no longer melee across a height gap: 
      Vanilla really does allow this; this now follows GZDoom, which refuses 
      a swing when the two bodies don't overlap vertically at all
    - melee reach now uses vanilla's real formula instead of a flat 72 units


===============================================================================

v0.10.0 (2026-08-08)

Features and improvements
  - the Icon of Sin (DOOM2 MAP30) works
  - Commander Keen (DOOM2 MAP32) works
  - add "You found a secret area" message
  - bullets and melee hits now splash blood
  - bullets now leave the original's puff on walls (and on barrels)
  - hopefully completed THINGs
    - add missing idle animations to some items and decorations
    - added the two techno lamps and all gore decorations, which weren't
      rendered at all before
    - the 1.4x size increase now only applies to pickups
      (ammo/health/armor/keys/powerups)
  - main menu overhaul
    - opens over the paused level instead of hiding it, and got a
      "Return to game" button next to it
    - "Gamre files" is now "New game" and asks for the difficulty, which
      left the Settings tab
    - the game WAD, add-ons and level you picked are remembered
      between sessions
    - reopening the menu keeps you on the tab you were last on

Testing
  - there are unit tests now ("npm test", Node's own runner, no dependencies):
    see docs/testing.md

Fixed bugs
  - massive combat fixes
    - fixed monster missiles detonating at the spot you stood when they were
      fired, instead of flying on until they hit something
    - fixed every missile - yours and theirs - dying in mid-air 2048 units
      out; that cap is vanilla's bullet range, and a missile has none
    - fixed monster bullets never missing
    - fixed your bullets never missing a monster the cursor was on: auto-aim
      only sets the shot's slope, so every pellet of a shotgun blast now
      flies its own spread angle and hits or misses on its own
    - every weapon number is now vanilla's own
    - fixed your bullets dying in mid-air 2048 units out; your bullets
      now reach 8192 like GZDoom's, while monster bullets keep vanilla's
      2048 and so still can't reach that far back
  - fixed the fog of war stopping 3000 units out when the camera frames
    about 5000, so anything between the two sat in the dark - a monster
    there was invisible, un-targetable and unhittable while shooting at you
  - fixed THINGs were shaded by whatever their sector's light was at spawn
    instead of tracking it live, so they went stale in any blinking,
    strobing or switch-triggered sector
    - in-flight projectiles and the arch-vile's warning flame had the 
      same bug while moving between differently-lit sectors
  - fixed a sector moved only by a boss death was left in the static render
    batch, so it was drawn twice once its mover mesh appeared (should fix E1M8)
  - fixed triggering a second mover on a sector that already had one running
    hijacked it instead of being ignored


===============================================================================

v0.9.1 (2026-08-07)

Features and improvements
  - drops of dead monsters are better visible (or, at all)
  - animated textures
  - decorative THINGs are now blocking
  - improved HUD
    - show current level stats (kills/items/secrets) and time
    - moved the current weapon between armor and ammo
    - highlight ammo type for the current weapon
    - mouse cursor is now a proper crosshair, which color also 
      reflects the players healt

Fixed bugs
  - a lift blocked by someone's headroom now backs down again
    immediately instead of stalling at the ceiling
  - moveable objects that end up touching no longer freeze
    in place forever - they can now work their way apart again
  - fixed crushers


===============================================================================

v0.9.0 (2026-08-06)

Features and improvements
  - SOUND! every sound effect comes out of the loaded WAD, with the original's
    own attenuation, stereo panning, channel priorities and random pitch wobble
    - add-ons can replace individual sounds, in the original DMX format or as
      Ogg/WAV/FLAC; a sound the WAD set lacks is silent rather than substituted
    - volume slider on the start menu (remembered between sessions), M mutes
  - player movement more like vanilla
    - straferunning
    - the player slides along angled walls instead of sticking to them
    - improved auto-aim
    - optional "Autorun" (Main Menu -> Settings)
  - implemented per-map boss-death specials
  - improved monsters
    - completed mancubus, arch-vile, revenant and pain elemental attacks
    - monster melee/ranged damage now matches vanilla's real dice instead of a
      softer tuned approximation
    - the cyberdemon's rocket splashes like the player's own
    - monster projectile speeds are vanilla's own now instead of eyeballed
    - monsters keep infighting when the player dies
  - the BFG now deals its real vanilla damage instead of a plain radius
    splash, complete with the green flash on whatever each ray hits
  - projectiles, explosions, teleport fog and the revenant's smoke trail are
    batched like map things now instead of one draw call each
  - some main menu polish
  - add error message if WebGL2 is not available / unable to initialize

Fixed bugs
  - fixed monster fireballs flying straight through their own species instead
    of harmlessly exploding on it
  - fixed closing doors could trap the player (or a monster) underneath instead
    of bumping back open
  - lifts, rising floors (including stairs) and non-crushing ceiling movers now
    stop instead of clipping through the player or a monster
  - explosions no longer damage the spider mastermind or cyberdemon
  - fixed a crash (frozen game) whenever a monster's attack-pose animation was
    still playing at the moment it resumed walking — only reachable by the
    arch-vile so far, but the underlying bug was in the shared sprite animator
  - fixed monster projectiles damaging through walls
  - fixed dead lost souls/pain elementals leaving a permanent floating corpse
    instead of vanishing
  - fixed monsters melee-attacking straight through the height gap of a raised
    ledge, since line-of-sight's floor/ceiling check sampled too coarsely to
    ever catch a step at melee range
  - fixed severe frame drops on larger maps related to fog of war


===============================================================================

v0.8.0 (2026-08-04)

Gameplay
  - all powerups work now: invulnerability, berserk, partial invisibility,
    radiation suit, computer area map and light amp visor, on vanilla's timers
    (incl. screen tints for invulnerability/suit, and monsters shooting wide
    while you're invisible)
  - backpack works now, and was invisible before (doomednum 8 had no sprite)
  - fist and chainsaw finally do damage (2-20, x10 for the fist with berserk)
Engine
  - MASSIVE performance optimizations (NUTS.WAD from ~2 fps to ~38 fps !!!)
  - add support for A LOT more linedef/sector specials! 
    Vanilla compatiblity should be complete now.
  - add attack & pain animations
  - improved lightning, we're now much closer to vanilla
  - wall/floor "fading" effect now also applies to awake monsters (still needs some tweaking)
  - fixed useable linedefs could be triggered from both sides
  - fixed a monster teleporting through a walk trigger ended up facing the
    wrong way (its landing angle got converted from degrees a second time)
  - fixed picking wrong player1 spawn if multiple player1 spawns are present
UI / HUD
  - new HUD strip showing which powerups are running and for how much longer
  - more accurate FPS counter
  - DEVMODE: add simple profiler overlay


